---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import LegalContent from '../../components/LegalContent.astro';
import { EMAIL } from '../../lib/contact';
import { useTranslations } from '../../i18n/utils';

const lang = Astro.currentLocale ?? 'pt';
const t = useTranslations(lang);
---

<Layout
  title={`${t('legal.privacidadeTitle')} — Astromidnight`}
  description={t('legal.privacidadeMetaDesc')}
>
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-28 pb-24 sm:pt-32">
    <LegalContent title={t('legal.privacidadeTitle')} updated={t('legal.updatedDate')}>
      <h2>1. Who processes your data</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller for data collected through this site is David Cruz,
        carrying out the Astromidnight activity as a sole trader, based in São Pedro
        da Gafanhoeira, Alentejo, Portugal (Tax ID: 205254128). For any
        question about your data, write to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What data we collect and why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact forms</strong> (general contact and rural stays): name,
          email and the message text, so we can reply to you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Session bookings</strong>: name, email and other data you fill in
          on the booking engine, to organize and confirm the session.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Shop purchases</strong>: delivery and payment data, collected and
          processed directly by the external checkout platform — it doesn't pass
          through our servers or get stored by us.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>We use the following third-party services to run the site and our services:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> — processes and forwards contact-form messages by email.</li>
        <li><strong>Cal.com / Cal.eu</strong> — booking engine and calendar; handles the data you fill in when booking a session.</li>
        <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — stores the list of prints available in the shop (doesn't collect personal data while browsing).</li>
        <li><strong>meteoblue</strong> — weather forecast widget embedded on the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (Google Ireland Limited) — site usage statistics, only after you accept the cookie notice.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each of these services has its own privacy policy, which applies to the data
        they process on Astromidnight's behalf. We do not sell or share your data
        with third parties for marketing purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
      <p id="cookies">
        We use Google Analytics to understand how the site is used (pages visited,
        where visits come from, aggregated data) — but only after you accept the
        cookie notice on your first visit; if you reject or ignore the notice,
        Google Analytics never loads. IPs are anonymized. You can change your mind
        at any time under "Manage cookies", in the site footer. More details in
        Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The booking engine (Cal.com/Cal.eu) and the weather widget (meteoblue),
        embedded on some pages, are essential to the site's operation and always
        load — they may set their own cookies when you use them, and we have no
        direct control over them.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Legal basis and retention period</h2>
      <p>
        We process your data based on the performance of a contract (when you book
        a session or buy a print) or on your consent (when you write to us on your
        own initiative). We keep contact and booking data for as long as necessary
        to provide the service and comply with tax obligations, and delete or
        anonymize it afterwards.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, erase or restrict the
        processing of your data, to request its portability, and to object to
        processing. To exercise any of these rights, write to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
        You also have the right to file a complaint with Portugal's National Data
        Protection Authority (<a href="https://www.cnpd.pt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cnpd.pt</a>).
      </p>

      <h2>7. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable measures to protect the data we process directly, but no
        transmission over the internet is 100% secure. We recommend not sharing
        sensitive data (such as payment card details) by email or through the
        contact form.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Minors</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not directed at minors under 16 for the purposes of directly
        collecting data. Sessions involving minors must be booked by a responsible
        adult.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy periodically. The version in force is always the
        one published on this page, with the update date shown at the top.
      </p>
    </LegalContent>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
